{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.PosDef","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.StarOrdered","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace.card_le_trace_of_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace.card_le_trace_of_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PsdDetOneTrace.lean#L130-L166","doc":"**The bound in every dimension.** A real PSD matrix of determinant `1` has\ntrace at least its dimension.\n\nThe eigenvalues are non-negative with product `1`, so none is zero, and\n`log x ≤ x − 1` summed over them gives `0 = Σ log λᵢ ≤ Σ λᵢ − d`. That is\nAM-GM, taken in the form whose Mathlib lemma is `Real.log_le_sub_one_of_pos`.\n\nEquality holds exactly at the identity (each `λᵢ = 1`); the `d = 2` case of\nthat is `eq_one_of_trace_eq_two` above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace.not_posSemidef_of_trace_lt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace.not_posSemidef_of_trace_lt_two","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PsdDetOneTrace.lean#L109-L114","doc":"**What the two together say**, in the form the probe uses: for a\ndeterminant-one real `2×2` matrix whose trace is *strictly below* `2`, being\nPSD is impossible. An elliptic `SL₂(ℝ)` element's powers all have determinant\none and trace at most `2`, so this is the exclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace.eq_one_of_trace_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace.eq_one_of_trace_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PsdDetOneTrace.lean#L86-L107","doc":"**The equality case.** Trace exactly `2` forces the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace.trace_ge_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace.trace_ge_two","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PsdDetOneTrace.lean#L69-L84","doc":"**The obstruction.** A real symmetric PSD `2×2` matrix of determinant `1`\nhas trace at least `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace.offdiag_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace.offdiag_symm","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PsdDetOneTrace.lean#L63-L67","doc":"A real PSD `2×2` matrix is symmetric in the off-diagonal entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace.diag_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace.diag_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PsdDetOneTrace.lean#L59-L61","doc":"The diagonal entries of a real PSD matrix are non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0}]}